+  ///////////////////////////////////
+  // Coprocessor instructions (XIF) //
+  ///////////////////////////////////
+  // An instruction whose major opcode is selected by XifOpcodes and that the decoder found illegal is
+  // sent to the coprocessor instead of trapping. It is handled like a multi-cycle MUL/DIV:
+  //   cycle 1 (rs3 only): port A reads rs3, latched
+  //   then              : xif_issue_valid with rs1/rs2 (forwarded) and rs3 until xif_issue_ready
+  //   then              : wait for the xif_result_valid pulse (latched, the coprocessor has no
+  //                       result_ready), write rd, done
